# DESCRIPTION

The `shell` service is rc(1) on the console: what is typed at the keyboard reaches it through kbdfs(4)'s `/dev/cons`, and what it and its programs write is shown by console(4).
It is Plan 9's boot console, where `rc` reads and writes `#c/cons`.

The launcher starts `rc` with no descriptors, and `rc` takes `/dev/cons` as its terminal: it prompts, reads a line at a time, and gives a program it runs the terminal while that program has its standard input.
kbdfs edits the line being typed and echoes it to the console.
`^D` on an empty line ends the input of the program that has the terminal, or else `rc`'s; `rc` then exits, and the launcher starts a new one.

The service is in kbdfs's note group, so Delete interrupts it: kbdfs throws away the line being typed and posts `interrupt` to the group, which ends the program `rc` is running, and `rc` prompts again.

Its manifest:

```text
service shell
program rc
notegroup kbdfs
programs
use env
mount /bin bootfs/bin
mount /lib/man bootfs/lib/man
mount /dev kbdfs
mount /dev devmgr/dev after
mount /net devmgr/net
mount /net net/net after
mount /net cs/net after
mount /net dns/net after
mount /proc proc
mount /mnt/plumb plumber
restart always
```

It runs where `rc` is built, which needs the full Swift toolchain.

# EXAMPLES

```rc
% ls /svc
% cat
typed lines come back
(Delete)
%
```

